AOF / medial-axis methods
Morteza Rezanejad's AOFSkeletons and MLV work supplies the AOF formulation
adapted in src/kernels.cpp and the signed-distance/skeleton reference methods.
Original notice: Copyright Morteza Rezanejad, McGill University, 2019.
https://github.com/mrezanejad/AOFSkeletons
Explicitly licensed original files use GPL-3.0-or-later. Their notices are
retained in LICENSES/MLV-GPL-notices.txt; see also Rezanejad et al. (2019),
Scene Categorization from Contours: Medial Axis Based Salience Measures.
The R implementation changes indexing, validation and native execution;
comparison details and intentional departures are recorded in docs/PARITY.md.

